### Endpoint bubbles

When `mapMarkerDirectionsPreview` is active (and not `movingToPoiId`), the overlay renders teardrop-shaped markers at route endpoints:

| Marker | Icon | Background | Position |
|---|---|---|---|
| Start | `cu/figma-export-icons/MapPinSimpleArea.svg` (dark-purple pin) | White circle | First projected point |
| Destination | `directions-icons/flag-pennant.svg` (dark-purple flag) | Lemon `#DCFF7D` circle | Last projected point |

Both have a triangular pointer beneath the icon circle. The start marker additionally has a lime ground ring.

When the user clicks the swap arrow in the directions panel, the icons mirror onto the opposite endpoints (geometry stays the same — only the icon `src` swaps). The `swapped` flag is read from `nav.mapMarkerDirectionsSwapped`. See `bird-eye-map-controls.mdc` for the state-lift and overlay wiring.

The lemon "current location" pulse marker (`InteractionBoxesOverlay` `userLocation` projectable) is **hidden** while the directions panel is open — the start bubble takes its place. Outside of the directions session it remains visible as the player's current-location indicator.

